WEBVTT

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:01.220
You're out.

00:02:18.870 --> 00:02:20.370
Hey, Frank, take this wheel.

00:02:20.510 --> 00:02:24.980
You get one of these?

00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:28.220
I got one.

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:29.890
What are you going to do about it?

00:02:39.788 --> 00:02:40.588
Keep that warning.

00:02:41.228 --> 00:02:41.768
If I were you.

00:03:07.036 --> 00:03:07.636
Tom Purdy.

00:03:08.284 --> 00:03:08.844
Who shot him?

00:03:08.964 --> 00:03:09.344
I don't know.

00:03:09.404 --> 00:03:10.804
The shot seemed to come from the Bonanza.

00:03:12.412 --> 00:03:13.512
That's their answer.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:15.220
R.P., take care of it.

00:03:26.908 --> 00:03:27.908
Thank you.

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:28.560
other killing.

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:30.000
What is it?

00:03:30.860 --> 00:03:31.420
Tom Purdy.

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:35.610
Dean, I want you to take a message.

00:03:35.710 --> 00:03:41.120
Write it in the form of a notice and send a copy to every name listed here.

00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:52.660
The time has come for us to stand together and fight for the peace and security of our own.

00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:58.380
Under present conditions, we have no alternative to take the law into our own hands.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:04.020
for a call upon each of you to appear tomorrow night at 8 o'clock at Twin Oaks.

00:04:05.630 --> 00:04:10.250
Come on. Find David Ross head of the vigilante committee. Get that?

00:04:11.780 --> 00:04:14.920
I got it. Now listen, Dave, you can't get away with this.

00:04:15.670 --> 00:04:17.980
Why, I thought you'd given up this vigilante idea.

00:04:18.580 --> 00:04:20.020
You know, you can't make your own laws.

00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:24.740
Vigilantes are going to enforce them. Find those when they're finished.

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:29.980
Dave's going through with...

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:34.960
this crazy vigilante idea if chasing killers and murderers out of the community is a crazy idea

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:40.340
and I'm willing to be crazy as your attorney let me point out that you're taking the law into your

00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:46.960
own hands you're making yourself legally responsible for an illegal act I wouldn't sign those if I

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:47.620
were you risk

00:05:06.430 --> 00:05:07.730
I'm not discounting a danger, men.

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:10.320
I know that we've got a tough fight on our hands.

00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:14.260
But wouldn't it be worthwhile to see Trails End cleaned up?

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:16.200
A decent place to live in.

00:05:17.660 --> 00:05:19.960
You wouldn't get a very good view of it from the cemetery.

00:05:20.600 --> 00:05:21.120
He's right.

00:05:21.260 --> 00:05:24.000
It would be suicide for us to try to bump that mob.

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:25.960
There ain't enough of us to do the job.

00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:27.900
We'd be outnumbered three to one.

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:29.720
I know that we're outnumbered.

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:31.360
But I'm expecting help.

00:05:31.700 --> 00:05:32.340
Who do you mean?

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:38.500
You must have met.

00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:39.100
I'm scared.

00:05:40.970 --> 00:05:41.450
Hi, boy.

00:05:43.510 --> 00:05:44.170
Hello, boy.

00:05:44.330 --> 00:05:44.550
Hi, Dave.

00:05:44.830 --> 00:05:45.170
Hiya.

00:05:45.430 --> 00:05:46.390
Dave, I hope we ain't late.

00:05:46.590 --> 00:05:47.590
We are just in time.

00:05:48.220 --> 00:05:50.720
The committee thinks we haven't a chance against that bunch in town.

00:05:50.980 --> 00:05:52.440
They're plenty tough.

00:05:53.310 --> 00:05:53.510
Tough?

00:05:54.090 --> 00:05:55.490
They're no tougher than a lot we've tackled.

00:05:55.980 --> 00:05:56.860
Well, what's your plan?

00:05:57.210 --> 00:05:57.470
Plan?

00:05:57.610 --> 00:05:58.470
We don't need any plans.

00:05:58.900 --> 00:05:59.980
Ride into town and start...

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:02.280
Shooting and keep on shooting until the last man's run out.

00:06:02.870 --> 00:06:03.590
What do you say, boys?

00:06:05.620 --> 00:06:06.640
Wait a minute, boys.

00:06:11.460 --> 00:06:12.920
Might be able to lick him with that plan.

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:15.560
Happy he won't be here to celebrate the victory.

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:20.250
I think the right way to do it, plan a surprise attack.

00:06:20.830 --> 00:06:21.870
Here's how we go about it.

00:06:31.550 --> 00:06:32.230
How do you know?

00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:33.360
I've seen him over the ridge.

00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:34.080
He's right behind me.

00:06:45.830 --> 00:06:46.590
He's a man, he's a cunt.

00:06:47.480 --> 00:06:48.880
Save the doors and get your cunt.

00:07:00.280 --> 00:07:07.930
The mantle's barricaded.

00:07:08.660 --> 00:07:09.620
Get rid of your torches.

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:13.340
All right, men, know what to do.

00:07:57.450 --> 00:07:58.680
Oh, wish I knew.

00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:04.440
Keep them busy.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:01.160
Stop your guns and don't turn around.

00:09:01.300 --> 00:09:02.440
Stop your guns. All of you.

00:09:34.280 --> 00:09:36.460
He gave you a chance to leave peaceably.

00:09:36.600 --> 00:09:37.880
But you wouldn't take it. Just a minute.

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:41.500
I'm a stranger here. I dropped in for a moment,

00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:42.840
and I got caught in the middle of this mess.

00:09:43.610 --> 00:09:45.310
That's true. I haven't seen you before.

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:47.860
If you have nothing against me, I'd like to stay in town.

00:09:50.220 --> 00:09:53.070
Right? You may remain. Get them out.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:01.820
Crosses the county line, our work will be over.

00:10:02.340 --> 00:10:03.580
The vigilantes will disband.

00:10:04.110 --> 00:10:06.770
We can all go back to our homes knowing that we've done a good job.

00:10:07.880 --> 00:10:10.280
Boys, you know how grateful I am.

00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:12.430
Saying thank you seems a little small.

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:13.700
Oh, forget it.

00:10:17.930 --> 00:10:20.090
Well, Dave, you're due for a big shock tomorrow.

00:10:20.270 --> 00:10:20.490
Why?

00:10:20.710 --> 00:10:22.370
We're coming over to pay back that money you loaned us.

00:10:22.530 --> 00:10:22.970
All right.

00:10:23.230 --> 00:10:24.290
Then I'll see you in the morning.

00:10:24.460 --> 00:10:25.320
And thanks again.

00:10:25.500 --> 00:10:25.800
Okay.

00:10:32.720 --> 00:10:35.070
You needn't thank me. I done him all right.

00:10:37.560 --> 00:10:40.100
I didn't do so bad myself.

00:10:40.460 --> 00:10:45.130
Seems a pity to bust up a sweet little racket like this.

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:50.020
I think you've got something there.

00:11:03.230 --> 00:11:04.270
Get your hands in the air.

00:11:12.720 --> 00:11:15.100
Aren't you a little old to be playing with dogs?

00:11:15.670 --> 00:11:18.180
Well, he's not mine.

00:11:18.520 --> 00:11:19.540
Lullaby is Elmer's daddy.

00:11:22.580 --> 00:11:23.280
Here's your receipt.

00:11:24.430 --> 00:11:25.290
Staying in town long?

00:11:25.570 --> 00:11:28.690
No, we'll be heading back for the ranch as soon as we get some supplies.

00:11:29.170 --> 00:11:29.890
Thanks again, Dave.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:32.080
Call on me anytime if I can help you.

00:11:32.400 --> 00:11:34.180
We'll call on you even if you can't help us.

00:11:35.350 --> 00:11:36.630
You, uh, you been working here long?

00:11:38.100 --> 00:11:39.620
I'll bet Dave's a great guy to work for, isn't he?

00:11:40.890 --> 00:11:43.410
But old poker puss McAllister, he must be a pain in the neck.

00:11:43.590 --> 00:11:45.470
Well, if that old crab ever laughed, he'd crack his face.

00:11:47.500 --> 00:11:48.480
Jean, come here.

00:11:51.660 --> 00:11:51.960
Father.

00:12:05.440 --> 00:12:06.000
Mac's daughter.

00:12:06.740 --> 00:12:07.520
Peter's like it.

00:12:08.350 --> 00:12:09.590
Why didn't somebody tell me?

00:12:09.750 --> 00:12:10.730
Why didn't you ask?

00:12:11.440 --> 00:12:13.620
I thought you said Stoney was a lady's man.

00:12:13.820 --> 00:12:14.960
Turn that thing off.

00:12:15.390 --> 00:12:17.290
All right, father, old sourpuss.

00:12:17.650 --> 00:12:19.030
Come on, let's get out of here.

00:12:30.440 --> 00:12:35.320
I thought Ross had disbanded his vigilantes.

00:12:35.420 --> 00:12:35.900
He did.

00:12:36.160 --> 00:12:37.080
This is a new outfit.

00:12:37.400 --> 00:12:40.820
We're just borrowing his idea and making it pay dividends.

00:12:43.500 --> 00:12:44.640
Who's ahead in this new outfit?

00:12:45.060 --> 00:12:49.000
I can't tell you his name, but he's one of the biggest men in this county.

00:12:49.310 --> 00:12:50.310
And plenty smart.

00:12:50.590 --> 00:12:52.150
I could use a little extra dough.

00:12:53.060 --> 00:12:53.720
Count us in.

00:12:55.390 --> 00:12:58.770
With our cut in the profits, we can retire in a year's time.

00:12:59.320 --> 00:12:59.980
Sounds all right.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:01.350
When are you getting started?

00:13:01.660 --> 00:13:03.420
We're holding our first meeting tonight.

00:13:04.300 --> 00:13:04.740
I'll be there.

00:13:07.940 --> 00:13:18.040
Give him the role.

00:13:21.410 --> 00:13:23.720
Now you'll be known as number 17.

00:13:25.940 --> 00:13:29.940
We've all been through the same ceremony, so we will now close the meeting.

00:13:30.960 --> 00:13:37.220
By taking our oath of allegiance, which will be given to us by our leader, number one.

00:13:41.920 --> 00:13:47.190
Do you solemnly swear to unquestioningly obey all orders issued by me, your leader?

00:13:48.390 --> 00:13:48.950
I am.

00:13:50.210 --> 00:13:57.950
Remember, once you have been initiated into the Purple Vigilantes, there is no turning back.

00:13:59.330 --> 00:13:59.970
Only...

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:02.360
Death can release you.

00:14:03.380 --> 00:14:05.100
To all of this, you solemnly swear,

00:14:06.520 --> 00:14:07.480
I will do.

00:14:57.200 --> 00:14:59.360
vigilante ideas proving a boomerang.

00:15:01.150 --> 00:15:06.600
We try to stamp out crime and only succeed in showing criminals a new way to break the law.

00:15:07.080 --> 00:15:09.420
Yeah, a smart way to cover up their tracks.

00:15:10.140 --> 00:15:13.080
By shifting the blame to the original vigilantes that you organized.

00:15:16.650 --> 00:15:18.930
This was found outside of Bascom's place.

00:15:24.160 --> 00:15:26.720
This is one of the notices I sent out six weeks ago.

00:15:27.070 --> 00:15:27.930
That's what I figured.

00:15:28.720 --> 00:15:29.980
It looks as though some of your...

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:37.680
original outfit was mixed up with this bunch. Any idea who they are? Slightly. I could have sworn that

00:15:37.680 --> 00:15:46.300
every man I picked was trustworthy. Yeah, maybe so. Dave, a lot of people are feeling pretty bitter

00:15:46.300 --> 00:15:52.440
against you. Some of them believe that you're still heading to vigilantes. Might be a good idea

00:15:52.440 --> 00:15:58.660
if you left town for a little while. I'm not in the habit of running away from trouble, Jim. What's the

00:15:58.660 --> 00:15:59.840
The sense of waiting for...

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:00.580
I'll catch up with you.

00:16:01.360 --> 00:16:02.440
You're imagining things.

00:16:02.720 --> 00:16:16.540
What do you need of all this?

00:16:16.760 --> 00:16:19.840
A little present for your partner, Dave Bross, and the rest of his purple killers.

00:16:20.380 --> 00:16:22.440
And tell him the next time it won't be windows we'll break.

00:16:22.800 --> 00:16:24.100
I'll have the law on you for this.

00:16:29.110 --> 00:16:29.710
Imagination, eh?

00:16:30.860 --> 00:16:32.860
If I ran away, I'd be admitting my guilt.

00:16:33.250 --> 00:16:35.530
But, Dave, what's the sense of sticking your chin out?

00:16:35.970 --> 00:16:37.250
Why don't you take a little trip?

00:16:37.940 --> 00:16:40.920
No, I'm going to stay and get at the bottom of this.

00:16:42.760 --> 00:16:43.740
Thanks for the advice, Jim.

00:16:57.370 --> 00:16:58.800
Hello. Remember me?

00:17:00.190 --> 00:17:04.510
I do. You're the little boy who plays a doll.

00:17:05.950 --> 00:17:08.130
Lady, you never said a truer word.

00:17:12.340 --> 00:17:15.500
Luzon, Stoney, come on over here, boys.

00:17:16.150 --> 00:17:17.010
You too, lullaby.

00:17:17.620 --> 00:17:18.320
I'll see you later.

00:17:19.300 --> 00:17:19.580
You too.

00:17:22.530 --> 00:17:25.370
Dave stays here. Somebody with a grudge is going to get him.

00:17:26.180 --> 00:17:26.800
What can we do?

00:17:27.340 --> 00:17:28.840
Well, I thought you might talk to him.

00:17:29.390 --> 00:17:29.970
The only way...

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:35.920
get him out of town be to kidnap him yeah for arrest him there's an idea he'd be safe in jail

00:17:35.920 --> 00:17:41.310
wouldn't he not in this jail well couldn't you take him to the county seat or if there was a

00:17:41.310 --> 00:17:45.850
charge against him well that ought to be easy uh dave ross is head of the purple vigilantes

00:17:46.160 --> 00:17:54.830
fine let's make it good while we're at it sheriff i saw dave ross killed three defenseless men

00:17:54.830 --> 00:17:59.350
and robbed their widows how's that hold on sheriff

00:18:00.410 --> 00:18:01.510
I'm sure there won't be any kickback.

00:18:01.910 --> 00:18:02.790
Not a chance.

00:18:02.950 --> 00:18:04.690
I don't intend to file this complaint.

00:18:04.970 --> 00:18:07.130
All I want to do is get Dave out of town.

00:18:10.310 --> 00:18:10.690
Simon.

00:18:14.560 --> 00:18:14.880
Tracy.

00:18:15.970 --> 00:18:16.370
Tracy.

00:18:18.430 --> 00:18:20.330
I'm taking Ross over to the county seat.

00:18:20.510 --> 00:18:20.690
Right.

00:18:21.010 --> 00:18:22.770
You'll be in charge here until I get back.

00:18:22.870 --> 00:18:23.210
Yes, sir.

00:18:39.210 --> 00:18:39.590
Oh, Jim.

00:18:40.080 --> 00:18:45.890
Oi, misceteers have issued a complaint against you, Ross.

00:18:46.220 --> 00:18:48.060
I'll have to take you over to the county seat.

00:18:49.870 --> 00:18:52.740
So you're in on the plot to get me out of town, too.

00:18:53.130 --> 00:18:54.010
Be sensible, Dave.

00:18:54.130 --> 00:18:56.250
Your life isn't worth a plugged nickel around these parts.

00:18:56.410 --> 00:18:58.730
Just go along with the sheriff and give us a chance to clear things up.

00:19:00.410 --> 00:19:03.630
He hasn't any choice in the matter.

00:19:04.180 --> 00:19:06.160
I've got enough on Dave to hang him.

00:19:06.540 --> 00:19:08.960
A fine thing when your best friends frame you.

00:19:09.650 --> 00:19:10.370
I'll tell Mac.

00:19:14.820 --> 00:19:21.850
Mac, you're a prisoner.

00:20:04.570 --> 00:20:04.810
Yeah.

00:20:06.630 --> 00:20:07.860
Kick your heads, man.

00:20:09.760 --> 00:20:11.100
I didn't even see who fired the shot.

00:20:11.200 --> 00:20:12.040
I didn't have to say it.

00:20:12.100 --> 00:20:12.520
It was Ross.

00:20:12.740 --> 00:20:13.980
And hanging ain't good enough for him.

00:20:14.410 --> 00:20:15.010
See your gun.

00:20:21.540 --> 00:20:22.380
Hasn't been fired.

00:20:22.690 --> 00:20:23.890
One of his hired killers did it.

00:20:25.540 --> 00:20:27.620
Yeah, one of his sneaking vigilantes shot him.

00:20:31.340 --> 00:20:32.620
That complaint isn't on the level, Tracy.

00:20:32.860 --> 00:20:33.460
Just a minute.

00:20:34.764 --> 00:20:36.424
Well, that's just an excuse to get Ross out of town.

00:20:36.780 --> 00:20:38.480
Looks to me like it establishes a motive.

00:20:38.672 --> 00:20:39.212
Wait a minute.

00:20:39.596 --> 00:20:40.936
You've got to give us a chance to explain.

00:20:41.056 --> 00:20:43.036
You can do your explaining in court, Ross.

00:20:43.372 --> 00:20:44.292
You're under arrest.

00:21:01.244 --> 00:21:03.704
You realize, of course, the most damaging evidence against Dave.

00:21:04.348 --> 00:21:04.888
It's your complaint.

00:21:05.468 --> 00:21:06.748
We didn't explain all that.

00:21:07.100 --> 00:21:07.880
I expect you to.

00:21:08.412 --> 00:21:09.112
On the witness stand.

00:21:10.268 --> 00:21:13.248
I'm going to call each of you to testify regarding your interview with Sheriff Dyer.

00:21:14.460 --> 00:21:16.880
You know, Drake, I have an idea that somebody's in back of all this

00:21:16.880 --> 00:21:18.500
that wants Ross out of the way, and badly.

00:21:19.292 --> 00:21:21.852
If we only knew the reason why we have plenty to work on.

00:21:22.396 --> 00:21:23.896
I hope you boys realize...

00:21:23.996 --> 00:21:26.936
that we're depending on your testimony to clear Dave at the trial tomorrow.

00:21:27.452 --> 00:21:28.492
Now, don't fail us.

00:21:29.212 --> 00:21:29.872
We'll be there.

00:21:30.156 --> 00:21:30.996
Ah, good.

00:21:34.220 --> 00:21:34.720
I'll see you in the morning.

00:21:35.116 --> 00:21:35.476
Good night.

00:21:36.076 --> 00:21:36.416
Good night.

00:21:44.492 --> 00:21:45.892
Well, I've got a date. I'll see you fellas later.

00:21:46.284 --> 00:21:46.864
Nothing going.

00:21:47.212 --> 00:21:47.972
You're coming with us.

00:21:48.112 --> 00:21:49.572
We've got to start for quarter late in the morning.

00:21:53.452 --> 00:21:54.352
I want some breakfast.

00:21:54.552 --> 00:21:55.992
What a man, he's always hungry.

00:21:56.152 --> 00:21:58.112
We'll eat when we get to town, before court opens.

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:05.860
Let's get him.

00:22:05.980 --> 00:22:06.900
No, we haven't time.

00:22:07.140 --> 00:22:08.060
We've got to be in court by 10.

00:22:08.220 --> 00:22:09.760
This may be the only means of saving Dave.

00:22:10.060 --> 00:22:10.620
We can make it.

00:22:12.190 --> 00:22:12.970
We've got to be in court.

00:23:07.196 --> 00:23:08.196
Thanks for turning.

00:23:10.844 --> 00:23:12.064
Is it true, Mr. McAllister?

00:23:12.636 --> 00:23:13.436
that you were present

00:23:13.788 --> 00:23:14.988
When David Rothman...

00:23:15.196 --> 00:23:16.436
Hold a meeting of the vigilantes.

00:23:17.116 --> 00:23:17.376
What?

00:23:17.456 --> 00:23:17.656
Yeah.

00:23:18.524 --> 00:23:19.564
Answer yes or no.

00:23:20.092 --> 00:23:20.372
Bye-bye.

00:23:20.860 --> 00:23:21.220
Yes.

00:23:24.028 --> 00:23:25.188
This is David Ross signature.

00:23:26.844 --> 00:23:27.484
Yes, it is.

00:23:27.676 --> 00:23:28.156
It is.

00:23:28.572 --> 00:23:28.992
Thank you.

00:23:29.212 --> 00:23:29.592
McAllister.

00:23:30.156 --> 00:23:30.676
That's all.

00:23:42.636 --> 00:23:43.296
Like a truce.

00:23:44.044 --> 00:23:44.984
I reckon I've had enough.

00:23:45.772 --> 00:23:46.312
Yeah, maybe.

00:23:46.924 --> 00:23:48.084
And then again, maybe it's a trick.

00:23:48.652 --> 00:23:50.032
We'd better not take any chances.

00:24:02.940 --> 00:24:07.970
Oh, I reckon it's water light, boys.

00:24:08.680 --> 00:24:10.060
Are you mad hurt, Lullaby?

00:24:10.620 --> 00:24:17.010
Oh, take it easy, boys.

00:24:17.170 --> 00:24:18.010
It may be a trap.

00:24:20.620 --> 00:24:23.600
Hey, look, a horse!

00:24:31.692 --> 00:24:33.892
Gentlemen of the jury, have you agreed upon a verdict?

